@prefix : <http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/newsreportingevent.owl#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xml: <http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@base <http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/newsreportingevent.owl> .

<http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/newsreportingevent.owl> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                                      owl:imports <http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/reportingevent.owl> ,
                                                                                  <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/actingfor.owl> ,
                                                                                  <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeindexedsituation.owl> ;
                                                                      <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#coversRequirements> """
In addition to the competency questions defined for pattern
ReportingEvent (http:/ontologydesignpatterns.org/wiki/Submissions:ReportingEvent)
the pattern allows to answer the following questions:
- What aspects of an actual event were presented in the news message?
- Who reported an actual event? Which news provider they represented?
- When was a certain actual event reported for the first time?
- What actual events are presented in a certain medium/by media of a certain news provider?
- How was an actual event presented?
		"""@en ;
                                                                      <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#hasComponent> "http://ontologydesignpatterns.org/wiki/Submissions:ActingFor" ,
                                                                                                                                                          "http://ontologydesignpatterns.org/wiki/Submissions:IntensionExtension" ,
                                                                                                                                                          "http://ontologydesignpatterns.org/wiki/Submissions:ReportingEvent" ,
                                                                                                                                                          "http://ontologydesignpatterns.org/wiki/Submissions:TimeIndexedSituation" ,
                                                                                                                                                          "http://ontologydesignpatterns.org/wiki/Submissions:Types_of_entities" ;
                                                                      <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#hasConsequences> """
The pattern is rather complex and should only be used if the circumstances of the events presented in a media
are expected to be uncertain (to differ in different news event reports of different news providers).
		"""@en ;
                                                                      <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#hasIntent> """
The pattern can be used for modelling situations
in which we are not certain that a particular actual event has the properties
which were described in a news message. We want to define the properties
of an actual event which were reported (time, place, actors, subevents,
cause, effect etc.), but not to treat them as universal, verified knowledge.
The pattern also allows to define who is responsible for a particular
description of an event and how this description is dealt with.
		"""@en ;
                                                                      <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#relatedCPs> """
Pattern NewsReportingEvent is an extension of ReportingEvent pattern.

Pattern ActingFor (http:/ontologydesignpatterns.org/wiki/Submissions:ActingFor) is a component of this pattern.
It allows to model the fact that NewsEventReporter (Agent) acts for NewsProvider (SocialAgent).

TODO describe time indexed situation
		"""@en ;
                                                                      <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl#scenarios> """
A single actual event, bus drivers protest, is presented in to different media: a TV news station
and a news website. John Doe prepared the material for the station Channel 55, owned by Media Corp.
This material was presented as first material in a news programme on 16/07/2016, started at 19:30 and ended at 19:35.
It was based on correspondent report. The material said that the cause of the protest was malfunction of buses,
and that a brutal police intervention took place.

The article from website livingintheworld.com also mentioned malfunction of buses, but it also mentioned
other cause of protest: planned reduction of social benefits. It did not mention brutal police intervention,
but it did mention destruction of public property. The article seems not important for the website authors,
it was presented at the page bottom.
		"""@en ;
                                                                      rdfs:comment "Pattern description is available at: http://ontologydesignpatterns.org/wiki/Submissions:NewsReportingEvent"@en ,
                                                                                   "Pattern description is included in: E. Kowalczuk, A. Ławrynowicz, \"The Reporting Event Ontology Design Pattern and Its Extension to Report News Events\" (2016)."@en ,
                                                                                   "This ontology is a formalisation of the News Reporting Event ontology design pattern."@en .

#################################################################
#    Object Properties
#################################################################

###  http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/newsreportingevent.owl#hasPresentationContext
:hasPresentationContext rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                        rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/situation.owl#isSettingFor> ;
                        rdfs:range :PresentationContext ;
                        rdfs:comment "This property can be used to link NewsReportingEvent to a NewsPresentationContext."@en .


###  http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/newsreportingevent.owl#owns
:owns rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
      rdfs:comment """This property can be used to link a certain NewsProvider with a Media that the NewsProvider ows, e.g. Fox News Channel is owned by Fox Entertainment Group, which also owns other Media (FXX Channel, etc.).
This is an universal property, it can be also used in different context (e.g. Ruslana owns a Persian cat)."""@en .


###  http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/newsreportingevent.owl#presentedAt
:presentedAt rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
             rdfs:comment """This property can be used to link a NewsReportingEvent to a Media (TV station, radio station, newspaper, webpage) at which a certain ActualEventView was presented. 
This is an universal property and can be used in different contexts."""@en .


###  http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/reportingevent.owl#hasAuthor
<http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/reportingevent.owl#hasAuthor> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty .


###  http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/reportingevent.owl#reports
<http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/reportingevent.owl#reports> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeindexedsituation.owl#forEntity> .


#################################################################
#    Classes
#################################################################

###  http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/newsreportingevent.owl#Media
:Media rdf:type owl:Class ;
       rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/typesofentities.owl#Object> ,
                       [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                         owl:onProperty [ owl:inverseOf :owns
                                        ] ;
                         owl:qualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
                         owl:onClass :NewsProvider
                       ] ;
       rdfs:comment "An entity that allows a communication of news messages, for example a TV station, radio station, newspaper, website, etc."@en .


###  http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/newsreportingevent.owl#NewsEventReporter
:NewsEventReporter rdf:type owl:Class ;
                   rdfs:subClassOf <http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/reportingevent.owl#EventReporter> ,
                                   <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/actingfor.owl#Agent> ,
                                   [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                     owl:onProperty [ owl:inverseOf <http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/reportingevent.owl#hasAuthor>
                                                    ] ;
                                     owl:someValuesFrom :NewsReportingEvent
                                   ] ;
                   rdfs:comment """An Actor (usually a Person) that is an author of a certain ActualEventView.
NewsEventReporter is not linked to an ActualEventView directly, it is connected to NewsReportingEvent, which is designed to document the act of reporting."""@en .


###  http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/newsreportingevent.owl#NewsPresentationContext
:NewsPresentationContext rdf:type owl:Class ;
                         rdfs:subClassOf :PresentationContext ,
                                         [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                           owl:onProperty [ owl:inverseOf :hasPresentationContext
                                                          ] ;
                                           owl:someValuesFrom :NewsReportingEvent
                                         ] ;
                         rdfs:comment """Class for denoting circumstances of an actual event presentation. For example if an event was presented at the end of website, then end of website is its NewsPresentationContext.
NewsPresentationContext is not directly attached to an ActualEventView, it is attached to NewsReportingEvent, which designates the act of an event reporting."""@en .


###  http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/newsreportingevent.owl#NewsProvider
:NewsProvider rdf:type owl:Class ;
              rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/actingfor.owl#SocialAgent> ,
                              [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                owl:onProperty :owns ;
                                owl:someValuesFrom :Media
                              ] ;
              rdfs:comment "An entity, usually a company, that ows a certain Media. For example Fox Entertainment Group owns the Fox News Channel. Fox Entertainment Group is a NewsProvider."@en .


###  http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/newsreportingevent.owl#NewsReportingEvent
:NewsReportingEvent rdf:type owl:Class ;
                    rdfs:subClassOf <http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/reportingevent.owl#ReportingEvent> ,
                                    <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/timeindexedsituation.owl#TimeIndexedSituation> ,
                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty :presentedAt ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom :Media
                                    ] ,
                                    [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                      owl:onProperty <http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/reportingevent.owl#hasAuthor> ;
                                      owl:someValuesFrom :NewsEventReporter
                                    ] ;
                    rdfs:comment "This is a subclass of ReportingEvent, designed to represent an act of reporting a certain actual event during a news programme or via other news media."@en .


###  http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/newsreportingevent.owl#PresentationContext
:PresentationContext rdf:type owl:Class ;
                     rdfs:subClassOf <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/typesofentities.owl#Entity> ;
                     rdfs:comment "Class for denoting circumstances of an entity presentation. If a waiter presented a dish with an apologetic smile, then the apologetic smile is a PresentationContext."@en .


###  http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/reportingevent.owl#EventReporter
<http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/reportingevent.owl#EventReporter> rdf:type owl:Class .


###  http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/reportingevent.owl#ReportingEvent
<http://semantic.cs.put.poznan.pl/ontologies/reportingevent.owl#ReportingEvent> rdf:type owl:Class .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/typesofentities.owl#Entity
<http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/typesofentities.owl#Entity> rdf:type owl:Class .


###  http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/typesofentities.owl#Object
<http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/cp/owl/typesofentities.owl#Object> rdf:type owl:Class .


